#
# The third-party images a trust node runs, mirrored into ghcr.io/londonaicentre/mirror/<name> so a
# site allowlists one registry (FLIP#1721). Each line is the upstream reference and the digest of its
# image index; scripts/mirror_images.sh copies that digest (a byte-identical index, so the mirror has
# the same digest) and tags it with the upstream tag. The compose files, the Helm chart and the
# Ansible seed role pin `ghcr.io/londonaicentre/mirror/<name>:<tag>@<digest>`;
# scripts/tests/test_mirror_images.py keeps them on this list.
#
# Bumping a version: `docker buildx imagetools inspect <upstream>` for the new digest, update the line
# and every pin, then `gh workflow run mirror_images.yml --ref <branch>` (or `make mirror-images` with
# a write:packages login) before the PR merges, so no branch names a mirror that does not exist yet.
# Loki and Grafana are AGPL-3.0: each mirror's package description links to its upstream source.
#
# <upstream>  <index digest>
docker.io/grafana/loki:3.4.0  sha256:74b8ccbd6e4b4932874742cf3997389592389ea721b3f210aad266486b985a4c
docker.io/grafana/alloy:v1.9.0  sha256:32bc0ba6bad75ca24bdf4a6d2dd793a564dff06b6446927699c08d9f9c749c6e
